(Title) Tj
T*
(Vascular stiffness and inflammatory response to adjunctive low-dose anti-inflammatory) Tj
T*
(therapy in hypertensive patients: results from the COHERENT trial) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Abstract) Tj
T*
(Background: Inflammation and arterial stiffening are implicated in hypertension) Tj
T*
(pathophysiology. This double-blind, placebo-controlled trial evaluated whether adjunctive) Tj
T*
(low-dose anti-inflammatory therapy reduces vascular dysfunction in hypertensive patients.) Tj
T*
(Methods: 150 hypertensive adults \(mean age 64.5 years, mean systolic BP 140 mmHg\) were) Tj
T*
(randomized 1:1 to receive adjunctive 0.5 mg daily anti-inflammatory agent \(n=75\) or) Tj
T*
(placebo \(n=75\) for six months, alongside standard blood pressure medications. Primary) Tj
T*
(endpoint was change in carotid-femoral pulse wave velocity. Secondary endpoints included) Tj
T*
(office and ambulatory blood pressure, echocardiographic parameters, and serum inflammatory) Tj
T*
(and cardiac biomarkers. Results: At six months, the treatment group demonstrated) Tj
T*
(numerically greater reduction in pulse wave velocity compared to placebo; however,) Tj
T*
(statistical significance was not achieved \(between-group difference -0.34 m/s, 95% CI) Tj
T*
(-0.89 to 0.21\). Blood pressure reduction was comparable between groups. Secondary analyses) Tj
T*
(showed modest reductions in high-sensitivity C-reactive protein in the treatment arm. Left) Tj
T*
(ventricular mass and other echocardiographic parameters did not differ significantly.) Tj
T*
(Conclusions: In hypertensive patients without established cardiovascular disease,) Tj
T*
(adjunctive low-dose anti-inflammatory therapy did not produce significant improvements in) Tj
T*
(arterial stiffness or other measured cardiovascular parameters over six months.) Tj
